{"attribution":{"text":"Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)","photos":"Wikimedia Commons, see each photo","thumbs":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/","width":500},"marinas":{"1239":{"n":"Portul Turistic Tomis","p":[["2/20/Constanta%2C_lighthouse.jpg","Constanta, lighthouse","Krzysztof Dudzik-Górnicki (User:ToSter)","CC BY-SA 3.0",1.33],["f/f6/Cazinoul_Constan%C8%9Ba_-_lateral_dreapta.jpg","Cazinoul Constanța - lateral dreapta","claudiu nh","CC BY-SA 2.0",0.62],["f/f8/Comandamentul_Marinei_-_Constanta_-_panoramio.jpg","Comandamentul Marinei - Constanta","Photopro Pro","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75],["e/e9/Faleza_Constanta_-_panoramio.jpg","Faleza Constanta","Photopro Pro","CC BY-SA 3.0",1.33],["3/39/Bust_of_Mihai_Eminescu_in_Constan%C5%A3a_%286145251106%29.jpg","Bust of Mihai Eminescu in Constanţa","Alexandru Panoiu from Bucharest, Romania","CC BY 2.0",0.67],["e/e0/Bust_of_Vasile_Urseanu_next_to_Fleet_Command_-_panoramio.jpg","Bust of Vasile Urseanu next to Fleet Command","Artem Korzhimanov","CC BY 3.0",0.67]],"a":["Tomis (castra)","Tomis was a Roman fort in the ancient city of Tomis (Constanța) in the Roman province of Moesia. According to the Tabula Peutingeriana it is situated between Stratonis and Histriopolis."]},"3140":{"n":"Marina Eforie","p":[["0/08/Eforie_Nord%2C_beach.jpg","Eforie Nord, beach","Krzysztof Dudzik-Górnicki (User:ToSter)","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75],["e/e7/Eforie_Nord_-_aug_2014_%281%29.JPG","Eforie Nord - aug 2014 (1)","Razvan Socol","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.66],["c/c7/Jet_ski_at_Eforie_Nord%2C_Romania_%281%29.JPG","Jet ski at Eforie Nord, Romania (1)","Razvan Socol","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.56],["0/00/Eforie_Nord_train_station_-_panoramio.jpg","Eforie Nord train station","jeffwarder","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75],["e/ea/FRUMUSETEA_MARII..._-_panoramio.jpg","FRUMUSETEA MARII...","chilipirea tatiana","CC BY 3.0",0.75],["3/36/Rasarit_.jpg","Rasarit","DariDaryk","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.56]],"a":["Eforie","Eforie (Romanian pronunciation: [efoˈri.e]; historical names (for Eforie Sud): Băile Movilă, Carmen-Sylva, Vasile Roaită) is a town and a holiday resort on the Black Sea shore, in Constanța County, Northern Dobruja, Romania. It is located about 14 km (8.7 mi) south of Constanța. Techirghiol Lake lies nearby."]},"3286":{"n":"Green Village Marina","p":[["e/e0/Falco_vespertinus_%28Falconidae%29_%28Red-footed_Falcon%29_-_%28male_adult%29%2C_Tulcea%2C_Romania.jpg","Falco vespertinus (Falconidae) (Red-footed Falcon) - (male…","This image is created by user Wouter va…","CC BY 3.0",0.58],["9/91/Biserica_din_Sf%C3%A2ntu_Gheorghe.jpg","Biserica din Sfântu Gheorghe","Grazie75","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.75],["6/68/Camping_Green_Village.jpg","Camping Green Village","Grazie75","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.56],["7/7e/20230425.Donau_Delta_Sf%C3%A2ntu_Gheorghe.-038.3.jpg","20230425.Donau Delta Sfântu Gheorghe.-038.3","Bybbisch94, Christian Gebhardt","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.62],["2/21/20230425.Sf%C3%A2ntu_Gheorghe_Iany_Melano.-203.jpg","20230425.Sfântu Gheorghe Iany Melano.-203","Bybbisch94, Christian Gebhardt","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.67],["3/34/Convolvulus_persicus_Sfantu_Gheorghe_1.jpg","Convolvulus persicus Sfantu Gheorghe 1","Xulescu g","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.67]],"a":["Sfântu Gheorghe branch","The Sfântu Gheorghe branch is a distributary of the river Danube, that contributes in forming the Danube Delta.\nThis is the southernmost branch of the Danube; the other two main branches are the Chilia branch and the Sulina branch. The Sfântu Gheorghe branch runs on a length of 64 kilometres (40 mi), in a southeasterly direction. Its outflow comprises about 22% of the Danube's discharge."]}}}